<title>UK: Euro cotton mart mulls EU duty decision.</title>
<headline>Euro cotton mart mulls EU duty decision.</headline>
<dateline>LIVERPOOL 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European textile industry continued to debate the implications of a European Union decision not to extend anti-dumping duties on grey cloth from certain countries.</p>
<p>Aside from strong French objections, observers in Italy reported pessimism regarding the impact on cotton industry prospects.</p>
<p>The anti-dumping duties, though provisional, were cited in the past few months in several markets as among factors contributing towards improved levels of sales activity for local enterprises.</p>
<p>But attempts to raise yarn prices have met little success and it is this consideration that now appears to be restricting the volume of business in raw cotton.</p>
<p>Demand remains focussed on the June/October shipment period but sellers' asking prices remain above the levels that many spinners are willing to pay just now.</p>
</text>
